                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ugh.  This is what happens when you give someone GameMaker and let them fool around for a little bit.  They make something like this.  It oozes amateur in every pore of the game, from the game crashes to the lack of direction on how to play it, and to the gameplay itself.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LZUNlVWeKX4\n\nI scored this game at a 10%, where the low cost of this game makes up almost half the score and it still couldn't muster even a respectable score on my first impressions look at it.  I did leave the developer some constructive criticism in my video review, so it's not all just negative stuff and kicking the lone indie developer.\n\nWhile this game shows promise that the developer might someday be able to put together a fun game, this isn't even close.. and it shouldn't be on Steam at any price, period.  Not recommended.  Avoid this, even if it's 10 cents on sale, sorry dev.",
